            <ArticleTitle>Particle size of inhaled corticosteroids: does it matter?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S88-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaci.2009.09.050</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A question with respect to asthma therapy revolves around the issue of whether better efficacy occurs with an ultrafine-particle inhaled corticosteroid because of better lung deposition into the distal airways. This article reviews particle size and delivery devices of different steroids, clinical outcomes of small- versus large-particle steroids, and the issue of pharmacoeconomics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
